[1] Construction A: H = diag(0,1,2,...);  H_a = transplant e_N -> eps, tail shifted down
    N_a = round(1/a), eps_a = a.   Delta_cont = 1.

    a          N      eps        Delta_a    d_H(H_a,H)  d_H(naive)  ker_dim  max_mult
    1.0e-01    10     1.0e-01    1.0e-01    1.0e-01     1.0e+00     1        1       
    1.0e-02    100    1.0e-02    1.0e-02    1.0e-02     1.0e+00     1        1       
    1.0e-03    1000   1.0e-03    1.0e-03    1.0e-03     1.0e+00     1        1       
    1.0e-04    10000  1.0e-04    1.0e-04    1.0e-04     1.0e+00     1        1       

    => Delta_a = eps_a -> 0  while Delta_cont = 1:  liminf Delta_a = 0 < 1 = Delta_cont.
    => d_H = eps_a -> 0 for the shifted family (Hausdorff convergence HOLDS).
    => the naive transplant has d_H = 1 (hole at N): the tail shift is what saves Hausdorff.
    => every eigenvalue is simple (max_mult = 1) and ker H_a = R e_0 (ker_dim = 1).

